                <pb facs="0321" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.5045/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-15T14:00:00-05:00">December 15, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>116. All quiet. <hi rendition="#italic">Galveston</hi> arrived Port-au-Prince
                    this morning. I have requested <hi rendition="#italic">Galveston</hi> to sail
                    afternoon 16th to arrive [Gonaives?] morning of 17th, sail from Gonaives noon
                    17th when she will be released from duty in Haitian waters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
